---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "The definite and zero article · A1 Grammar",
  "slug": "definite-and-zero-article",
  "level": "A1",
  "topic": "The definite and zero article",
  "category": "Grammar",
  "contentType": "grammar",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Choose the for an identifiable person or thing, and use no article for general plurals, uncountable ideas, and common daily chunks.",
  "sequence": 20,
  "prerequisites": ["a0/articles-a-an", "a0/regular-plural-nouns", "a1/present-simple"],
  "related": ["a1/there-is-there-are", "a1/some-any-with-countable-and-uncountable-nouns", "a1/daily-routines-and-telling-the-time"],
  "assessments": [
    "a1-exit"
  ],
  "tutorReviewRequired": true,
  "qualityReview": {
    "status": "editorial-review",
    "generatedPedagogy": true,
    "learnerPilotCount": 0,
    "scoredItemCount": 52,
    "revisionSummary": "Known reference, general plurals and uncountables, daily fixed chunks, transfer errors, spoken form, feedback, production, and retrieval were audited; three learner pilots remain."
  }
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="45–55 minutes" data-extension-duration="10–15 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 20</p>
  <h1><em>The</em> or no article?</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Help the listener identify a particular person or thing with <span class="ex">the</span>. Leave the space empty when you mean things in general: <span class="ex">The coffee on my desk is cold</span>, but <span class="ex">Coffee helps me wake up</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">45–55 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">known or general?</span>
    <span class="tag">the or no article</span>
    <span class="tag">10–15 min optional listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Follow one person through a normal workday.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Decide what the listener can identify.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose the, no article, and fixed daily chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Give a clear update about a fictional day.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">The central decision is not “Which noun always takes <span class="ex">the</span>?” Ask instead: “Can my listener identify the person or thing I mean?” Use <span class="ex">the</span> when the answer is yes. Use no article with plural or uncountable nouns when you mean the whole idea in general.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. A singular countable noun needs a marker, while a plural noun can stand alone when the meaning is general.">
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use <b>a</b>, <b>an</b>, or the plural form. Answer from memory, then check.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Retrieval answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="a">a</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="an">an</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="emails">emails</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>One new coworker is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="an" data-hint="Engineer begins with a vowel sound." data-fix="One new coworker is an engineer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> engineer. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(a / an)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I received <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="a" data-hint="Message is one new singular countable thing and begins with a consonant sound." data-fix="I received a message this morning." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> message this morning. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(a / an)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Our team sends many <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="emails" data-hint="Many requires a plural countable noun." data-fix="Our team sends many emails every day." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> every day. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(regular plurals)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Leila’s first morning at work</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“I met a manager at reception. The manager showed me the kitchen and the printer. I usually go to work by bus. I have lunch at one. Coffee helps me focus, but the coffee in the office is terrible.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Why does the speaker first say <span class="ex">a manager</span>, then <span class="ex">the manager</span>?</li>
      <li>Which kitchen, printer, and coffee can the listener identify?</li>
      <li>Where does English use no article before <span class="ex">work</span>, <span class="ex">bus</span>, <span class="ex">lunch</span>, and general <span class="ex">coffee</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. The points to an identifiable reference; no article presents a general plural or uncountable idea or completes a fixed daily chunk.">
    <h3>Discovery check: choose <em>the</em> or no article</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint"><b>Ø</b> means no article. Read the context before choosing.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Article choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the">the</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Ø">Ø</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I received an email this morning. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="The email was just introduced, so the listener can identify it." data-fix="The email was from my manager." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> email was from my manager.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>I read email all day at work. In general, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Email here means the uncountable activity or medium in general." data-fix="Email takes a lot of my time." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> email takes a lot of my time.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>These are the dogs next door. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="Next door identifies a particular group of dogs." data-fix="The dogs next door bark at night." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> dogs next door bark at night.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>This is a general fact about the animal. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Plural dogs means dogs as a whole class here." data-fix="Dogs need exercise." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> dogs need exercise.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>This is my normal weekday: I go to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Go to work is a fixed everyday chunk with no article." data-fix="I go to work at eight." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> work at eight.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I am going to one specific office today. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="Office is identified by the phrase on King Street." data-fix="The office on King Street opens at nine." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> office on King Street opens at nine.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: guide the listener</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>English articles help the listener build a picture. A new singular countable noun often enters the conversation with <span class="ex">a / an</span>. Once both people can identify it, <span class="ex">the</span> points back to it.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>listener’s picture</th><th>article choice</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>one new thing</b></td><td>a / an</td><td>I saw <b>a</b> café near the station.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>now identifiable</b></td><td>the</td><td><b>The</b> café closes at six.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>identified by the situation</b></td><td>the</td><td>Please close <b>the</b> door. <span class="contraction">(the door here)</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>identified by words after it</b></td><td>the</td><td><b>The</b> file on your desk is mine.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">The</span> does not mean “important,” and it does not mean “all.” It means the listener has enough information to identify the reference.</p>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Two common transfer directions</h3>
    <p>If your first language often leaves this meaning unmarked, English <span class="ex">the</span> can disappear: <span class="ex">I opened file</span>. Rebuild the listener’s picture: <span class="ex">I opened the file you sent</span>.</p>
    <p>Other languages often use a definite article with a general idea. In everyday U.S. English, a general plural or uncountable noun usually has no article: <span class="ex">I like coffee</span> and <span class="ex">Dogs need exercise</span>, not <span class="ex">I like the coffee</span> or <span class="ex">The dogs need exercise</span> when you mean all coffee or dogs in general.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>General meaning: plural and uncountable nouns</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Use no article before a plural countable noun or an uncountable noun when you mean the idea in general. Add <span class="ex">the</span> when the context identifies a particular group or amount.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>general, no article</th><th>identifiable, the</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Meetings can be tiring.</td><td>The meetings this week are long.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Phones are useful.</td><td>The phones on this desk are new.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Information is useful.</td><td>The information in this email is useful.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Music helps me work.</td><td>The music in this café is loud.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Do not remove the article from one singular countable noun. Say <span class="ex">A phone is useful</span> or <span class="ex">The phone on my desk is useful</span>, not <span class="ex">Phone is useful</span>.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. General plurals and uncountables take no article; an identifying phrase or shared situation makes the reference definite.">
    <h3>Drill 1: general or identifiable?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Choose <b>the</b> or <b>Ø</b>. The words after the noun often tell you whether the listener can identify it.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="General or identifiable article choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the">the</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Ø">Ø</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>In general, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Customers means customers as a general group." data-fix="Customers appreciate quick answers." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> customers appreciate quick answers.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We are discussing one store: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="At this store identifies a particular group of customers." data-fix="The customers at this store are waiting." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> customers at this store are waiting.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>As a general idea, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Advice is uncountable and general here." data-fix="Advice can be helpful." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> advice can be helpful.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>You sent me some advice yesterday. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="You sent me yesterday identifies the particular advice." data-fix="The advice you sent me yesterday was helpful." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> advice you sent me yesterday was helpful.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>In general, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Public transportation is an uncountable general system here." data-fix="Public transportation saves money." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> public transportation saves money.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>We are discussing one city: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="In this city identifies one transportation system." data-fix="The public transportation in this city is reliable." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> public transportation in this city is reliable.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>As a general preference, I like <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Coffee means the drink in general." data-fix="I like coffee." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> coffee.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>This cup is too bitter. I do not like <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="In this cup identifies one particular amount of coffee." data-fix="I do not like the coffee in this cup." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> coffee in this cup.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>High-frequency chunks with no article</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Some everyday meanings are stored as whole chunks. Learn the complete chunk, not a separate rule for each noun.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>meaning</th><th>no-article chunk</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>meals as routine events</b></td><td>have breakfast / lunch / dinner</td><td>We have lunch at noon.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>transport after by</b></td><td>by bus / train / car / plane</td><td>She goes to work by train.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>normal purpose</b></td><td>go to work / school / bed</td><td>They go to school at eight. I go to bed at eleven.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>The noun can still become identifiable</h3>
    <p>Compare the normal activity with a particular event or place:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">We have lunch at noon.</span> But: <span class="ex">The lunch we ordered is here.</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">I go to work by bus.</span> But: <span class="ex">I take the bus at 7:30.</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">The children go to school.</span> But: <span class="ex">I went to the school to meet their teacher.</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">I go to bed at eleven.</span> But: <span class="ex">My phone is on the bed.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Meals, by plus transport, and normal-purpose work, school, and bed chunks use no article; identifiable events and objects take the.">
    <h3>Drill 2: complete the daily chunk</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Choose <b>the</b> or <b>Ø</b>. Read the reason before the sentence.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Daily chunk article choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the">the</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Ø">Ø</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>This is my normal meal time: I have <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Have lunch is the normal meal chunk." data-fix="I have lunch at one every day." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> lunch at one every day.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We are discussing one order: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="We ordered identifies one particular lunch." data-fix="The lunch we ordered is ready." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> lunch we ordered is ready.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>This is her normal commute: She goes by <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="After by, the transport name has no article." data-fix="She goes by train." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> train.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>We mean the 7:15 service: She takes <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="Take the train refers to an identifiable service or means of transport." data-fix="She takes the 7:15 train." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> 7:15 train.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>This is his normal weekday activity: He goes to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Go to work is a fixed normal-purpose chunk." data-fix="He goes to work at eight." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> work at eight.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>They are visiting one building for a meeting: They went to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="For the meeting identifies one particular office building." data-fix="They went to the office for the meeting." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> office for the meeting.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>This is the child’s normal activity: Maya goes to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Ø" data-hint="Go to school means participate in the normal activity of being a student." data-fix="Maya goes to school from Monday to Friday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> school from Monday to Friday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The parent is visiting a known building: Maya’s father is at <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the" data-hint="The parent is at the particular school building for a meeting." data-fix="Maya’s father is at the school for a meeting." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> school for a meeting.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-success-message="Correct. The meaning controls the article: general, identifiable, routine chunk, or by plus transportation.">
    <h3>Drill 3: match the sentence to the reason</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a reason, then tap the sentence it explains.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="general plural">general plural</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="identifiable reference">identifiable reference</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="routine chunk">routine chunk</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="by plus transport">by plus transport</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="general plural" data-hint="No particular meetings are identified." data-fix="Meetings take time: general plural." data-placeholder="Meetings take time.">Meetings take time.</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="identifiable reference" data-hint="This afternoon identifies a particular set of meetings." data-fix="The meetings this afternoon are online: identifiable reference." data-placeholder="The meetings this afternoon are online.">The meetings this afternoon are online.</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="routine chunk" data-hint="Go to bed names the normal purpose, not one object." data-fix="I go to bed at eleven: routine chunk." data-placeholder="I go to bed at eleven.">I go to bed at eleven.</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="by plus transport" data-hint="A transport name after by has no article." data-fix="We travel by plane: by plus transport." data-placeholder="We travel by plane.">We travel by plane.</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the contrast</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="coffee helps me focus" data-hint="The sentence means coffee in general, so begin directly with Coffee." data-fix="Build: Coffee helps me focus." data-success-message="Correct. General uncountable coffee begins with no article.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build a general statement</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence about coffee in general.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="focus">focus</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="coffee">Coffee</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="me">me</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="helps">helps</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the coffee on my desk is cold" data-hint="Begin with The because on my desk identifies one particular coffee." data-fix="Build: The coffee on my desk is cold." data-success-message="Correct. The phrase on my desk makes the coffee identifiable.">
    <h3>Drill 5: build an identifiable reference</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence about one particular coffee.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="cold">cold</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="my">my</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="coffee">coffee</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="desk">desk</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="on">on</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair transfer errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="file" data-hint="The phrase you sent identifies one particular file. Look immediately before that noun." data-fix="I opened the file you sent." data-why="Use the when the listener can identify the noun from the context or from the words after it.">
    <h3>Drill 6: restore the missing article</h3>
    <p>The message says “I opened file you sent.” Tap the word that needs <span class="ex">the</span> before it.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="opened">opened</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="file">file</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="you">you</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="sent">sent</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="the" data-hint="The speaker means meetings in general, not a particular set." data-fix="Meetings can be tiring." data-why="A general plural noun usually takes no article in English.">
    <h3>Drill 7: remove the extra article</h3>
    <p>The speaker makes a general statement: “The meetings can be tiring.” Tap the extra word.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">The</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="meetings">meetings</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="can">can</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="be">be</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="tiring">tiring</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="the" data-hint="Have lunch is a fixed routine chunk." data-fix="I have lunch at noon." data-why="Routine meal names normally have no article in the chunk have breakfast, lunch, or dinner.">
    <h3>Drill 8: repair the meal chunk</h3>
    <p>The speaker describes a normal schedule: “I have the lunch at noon.” Tap the extra word.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have">have</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the">the</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="lunch">lunch</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="noon">at noon</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: keep <em>the</em> light and linked</h3>
    <p>In ordinary speech, <span class="ex">the</span> is usually unstressed. Before a consonant sound, it normally sounds like /ðə/: <span class="ex">the bus</span>, <span class="ex">the file</span>. Before a vowel sound, it normally sounds like /ði/: <span class="ex">the office</span>, <span class="ex">the email</span>.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>phrase</th><th>spoken shape</th><th>main beat</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>the file</td><td>thuh-FILE</td><td>file</td></tr>
        <tr><td>the office</td><td>thee-OFF-ice</td><td>office</td></tr>
        <tr><td>coffee helps</td><td>COFF-ee-helps</td><td>coffee</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>No article means no extra word and no extra pause. Move directly into the noun: <span class="ex">Coffee helps</span>, <span class="ex">Meetings take time</span>, and <span class="ex">by bus</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read identifiable, general, and fixed-chunk listening check">
