  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Final production: give Leila’s first-day update.</b> Use the notes to speak for 45–60 seconds: one new manager, the manager’s help, the office kitchen, coffee in general, the coffee at work, lunch time, and transport. Make every article choice help the listener follow the story.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Build two contrasts:</b> Choose one plural noun and one uncountable noun. Make a general statement, then identify a particular example. <span class="ex">Books are expensive. The books for my class are online.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your normal day, if you want:</b> Say when you go to work or school, how you travel, when you have lunch or dinner, and when you go to bed. You can invent a routine instead. You never need to disclose your real workplace, school, or schedule.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Repair in conversation:</b> If you hear an unclear noun, ask yourself, “Can my listener identify it?” Repeat the sentence with <span class="ex">the</span>, <span class="ex">a / an</span>, or no article.</div>

